<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 18 September, from 96 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/trajan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trajan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">96 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,930 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Domitian is murdered and Nerva becomes emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Domitian was stabbed to death in a palace conspiracy, and the Senate chose the elderly Nerva to succeed him. Nerva's adoption of Trajan began the era of the 'Five Good Emperors'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">324 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,702 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantine defeats Licinius at Chrysopolis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Constantine's victory over his co-emperor Licinius at Chrysopolis, across the Bosporus from Byzantium, made him sole ruler of the Roman Empire. He soon refounded Byzantium as Constantinople.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1793 CE <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington lays the cornerstone of the US Capitol</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Washington laid the cornerstone of the Capitol in a Masonic ceremony. Congress first met in the unfinished building in November 1800.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1850 CE <span class="tih-ago">176 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Fillmore signs the Fugitive Slave Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Part of the Compromise of 1850, the act required citizens of free states to help return people who had escaped slavery, and denied them a jury trial. It turned many Northerners against slavery.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1970 CE <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jimi Hendrix dies in London aged 27</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Guitarist Jimi Hendrix died in London after taking barbiturates. In four years of fame he had transformed the electric guitar with his use of feedback, distortion and virtuoso technique.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
